{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Af ḥovev.</b> From the Aramaic root, like 'and you shall be My segullah' and 'amim' is Israel, like 'after you, Benjamin, among your peoples' (Psalms 68:28). 'Peoples' — they call the mountain." "<b>And all His holy ones.</b> The sons of Levi." "<b>In your hand.</b> For they surround the Ark." "<b>They gather to your foot.</b> They walk in your way. And the meaning of <b>'in your hand'</b> — that you guard them." "<b>Bearing your words.</b> For they teach the Torah, and they are the transmitters of the oral Torah." "<b>Yissa.</b> Each singular, even though they are many." "And the meaning of <b>'your words'</b> — that which you spoke they shall bear, for they are the bearers of the Torah. For they also bear the Ark." "And the meaning of <b>'yissa'</b> is like 'and you shall not bear (תשא) a false report' (Exodus 23:1)." "<b>Takku.</b> Without a vav. And one says it is from the word 'within,' as though they walk within your foot. And others say that the tav stands in place of the heh, like the tav of 'I have traced (תרגלתי) for Ephraim' (Hosea 11:3), meaning even if they are beaten for your sake they will not abandon your words — and this is far-fetched. And the correct interpretation is that it is like 'they were drawn (נמשכו),' and the meaning is that they go to the place where the Ark is, which is the footstool of HaShem's feet. And this is the blessing: that HaShem will be a wall of fire around Israel, and they will be His segullah, and the Levites shall instruct the Torah always."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The lemma is from Deut. 33:3. The second quotation (Psalms 68:28) uses 'amim for the tribes of Israel. The final phrase 'עמים הר יקראו' is textually difficult; translated hyper-literally.", 5 "He explains that the verb ישא is grammatically singular despite referring to a plural subject."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:27.149139626Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}